<!--
    Copyright (c) 2026 Splitwirez
    Licensed under the MIT License. See LICENSE-aero-theme-for-avalonia.txt in the Themes/Aero
    directory for the full text of the copyright notice and permission notice.
    Source: https://github.com/Splitwirez/aero-theme-for-avalonia at main = a705b7c0
            src/AeroAvalonia/ControlStyles/ListBoxItem.axaml
    Changes from upstream: THIS FILE IS A RE-KEYED COPY OF THAT ONE. There is no upstream
    ComboBoxItem - all nine branches were queried for ComboBox*.axaml and every one returned zero
    hits, and AVMAP/Controls.axaml:86-87 names the type only inside a commented-out block pointing
    at AeroAvalonia.Placeholders.Themes.Fluent, an assembly that does not exist here. The notice
    above is therefore not about a drop-down row upstream wrote; it is here because the ~50 lines
    below ARE upstream's ListBoxItem. Normalise tabs to four spaces, strip the comments, and every
    remaining line is that file's byte for byte except the six changes recorded here.
      1. RE-POINTED the converter xmlns from "using:AeroAvalonia.Converters" to
         "using:TanMenu.Wpf.Themes.Aero.Converters", and DELETED upstream's
         xmlns:ae="using:AeroAvalonia" (:3) - nothing in the file uses that prefix and the
         namespace does not exist in this assembly. Both edits are inherited from the vendored
         ControlStyles/ListBoxItem.axaml, whose own change list is where they were first recorded.
      2. RE-KEYED to ComboBoxItem: x:Key="{x:Type ComboBoxItem}", TargetType="ComboBoxItem".
         THIS IS WHY THE FILE EXISTS AT ALL. Avalonia's ComboBoxItem derives from ListBoxItem and
         adds exactly one IsFocused subscription and one automation-control-type override
         (decompiled from Avalonia.Controls 12.1.0, whole class), but it does NOT override
         StyleKeyOverride, so its style key is typeof(ComboBoxItem) and the vendored file's
         {x:Type ListBoxItem} theme cannot reach it. Without this copy the drop-down rows would
         keep Fluent's ComboBoxItem template inside an Aero-painted popup.
      3. RENAMED the converter resource key AeroListBoxItemInnerCornerRadiiConverter ->
         AeroComboBoxItemInnerCornerRadiiConverter (declaration and its one {StaticResource}), and
         its xmlns prefix aecnv -> aeconv. Naming only: the instance and its Amount="-1" are
         upstream's, and the rename keeps two dictionaries that AeroResources.axaml merges side by
         side from publishing the same x:Key.
      4. RENAMED the presenter PART_ContentPresenter -> ItemContentPresenter, at both of its sites
         (the ContentPresenter's x:Name and the :disabled selector). AVMAP/StyleTrailMix.axaml
         carries a :disabled rule targeting ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter; Task 3 had to
         narrow its subject away from upstream's app-wide ":is(TemplatedControl)" precisely because
         Fluent's ComboBoxItem used that name and Views/Settings/AppearanceCard.axaml.cs paints the
         font list's group captions itself. This rename removes the collision structurally, which
         is what §7 Task 6 asks for.
         THE COST, MEASURED NOT ASSUMED: ContentControl.RegisterContentPresenter compares
         presenter.Name against the literal "PART_ContentPresenter" and returns false otherwise, so
         ContentControl.Presenter stays null on our rows and the presenter hosts its own content in
         its own logical children instead of the item's (Avalonia.Controls 12.1.0,
         ContentPresenter.UpdateHost / GetEffectiveLogicalChildren). Nothing in the ComboBox path
         reads either: ComboBox.UpdateSelectionBoxItem takes the item's CONTENT, and text search
         does the same. Every row in this app carries a string.
      5. RE-POINTED the :disabled Foreground from SystemControlDisabledBaseMediumLowBrush - a
         FLUENT key, which the vendored ListBoxItem deliberately left in place because it resolves
         - to AeroDisabledForeground. The font combo's group captions are the only disabled rows in
         this app and AppearanceCard.axaml.cs now names the same key, so the row and the caption
         cannot drift apart.
      6. ADDED four Setters upstream's ListBoxItem does not have, all of which change the paint:
         Foreground="{AeroForeground}" and FontSize="{AeroFontSizeNormal}" pin what upstream leaves
         to inheritance, and HorizontalContentAlignment="Left" / VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
         replace ContentControl's registered defaults, which are Stretch on both axes (decompiled).
         The template forwards all four to the presenter with TemplateBindings that are upstream's.
    Whitespace and casing, the only other differences: upstream's tabs are four spaces here, and
    x:ClassModifier is "internal" rather than upstream's "Internal". Both forms are accepted by the
    XAML compiler; neither reaches the rendered control.
-->
<ResourceDictionary xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:aeconv="using:TanMenu.Wpf.Themes.Aero.Converters"
    x:ClassModifier="internal">

    <aeconv:AdjustCornerRadiusConverter x:Key="AeroComboBoxItemInnerCornerRadiiConverter" Amount="-1" />

    <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type ComboBoxItem}" TargetType="ComboBoxItem">
        <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemHoverBackground}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemHoverOuterBorderBrush}" />
        <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
        <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="2" />
        <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,2" />
        <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AeroForeground}" />
        <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource AeroFontSizeNormal}" />
        <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Left" />
        <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        <Setter Property="Template">
            <ControlTemplate>
                <!-- The near-invisible Panel fill is the row's hit-test surface, so the gap
                     between the text and the row's edge selects too. It is ListBoxItem's own. -->
                <Panel Background="#01000000">
                    <Border x:Name="OuterBorder"
                            BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                            BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                            CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}">
                        <Border x:Name="InnerBorder"
                                Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                BorderBrush="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemHoverInnerBorderBrush}"
                                BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                CornerRadius="{Binding #OuterBorder.CornerRadius, Converter={StaticResource AeroComboBoxItemInnerCornerRadiiConverter}, Mode=OneWay}" />
                    </Border>
                    <ContentPresenter x:Name="ItemContentPresenter"
                                      Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                      ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                      Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}"
                                      HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}" />
                </Panel>
            </ControlTemplate>
        </Setter>

        <!--  Resting State: no frame at all, which is what makes a plain list read as plain text  -->
        <Style Selector="^:not(:pointerover,:pressed,:selected,:focus)">
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#OuterBorder">
                <Setter Property="IsVisible" Value="False" />
            </Style>
        </Style>


        <!--  Selected State  -->
        <Style Selector="^:selected:not(:pointerover),^:pressed">
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#OuterBorder">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedOuterBorderBrush}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#InnerBorder">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedBackground}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedInnerBorderBrush}" />
            </Style>
        </Style>


        <!--  Selected PointerOver State  -->
        <Style Selector="^:selected:pointerover">
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#OuterBorder">
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedHoverOuterBorderBrush}" />
            </Style>
            <Style Selector="^ /template/ Border#InnerBorder">
                <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedHoverBackground}" />
                <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource AeroListBoxItemSelectedHoverInnerBorderBrush}" />
            </Style>
        </Style>


        <!--  Disabled State. The font combo's group captions are the only disabled rows in this
              app, and they are disabled precisely so they cannot be chosen.  -->
        <Style Selector="^:disabled /template/ ContentPresenter#ItemContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AeroDisabledForeground}" />
        </Style>
    </ControlTheme>
</ResourceDictionary>
